description:
About us
AgileEngine is an Inc. 5000 company that creates award-winning software for Fortune 500 brands and trailblazing startups across 17+ industries. We rank among the leaders in areas like application development and AI/ML, and our people-first culture has earned us multiple Best Place to Work awards.
If you're looking for a place to grow, make an impact, and work with people who care, we'd love to meet you!
About the role
This role focuses on driving AI-driven digital transformation for large enterprises by bridging strategy and execution at the executive level. You will influence high-impact initiatives, shape modernization efforts, and ensure technology delivers measurable business value. The opportunity stands out through its strong consulting mindset, close collaboration with senior stakeholders, and exposure to complex enterprise environments. It offers strategic ownership, professional growth, and periodic U.S. travel to build trusted, long-term partnerships.
What you will do

 Act as a trusted advisor to C-level and V-level executives within large enterprise organizations;
 Define and lead strategic initiatives related to digital transformation, modernization, and AI adoption;
 Partner with clients to shape AI strategies, identify high-impact use cases, and support the execution of these initiatives end-to-end;
 Bring a strong consulting mindset, helping organizations translate complex technical concepts into actionable business outcomes;
 Oversee account performance metrics and implement strategies for continuous improvement;
 Travel to the U.S. quarterly to meet clients and strengthen relationships.

Must haves

 Strong US consulting experience (6+ years of experience);
 Proven experience managing client relationships in the IT services or custom software development industry;
 Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to translate technical concepts into business value;
 Leverage prior experience within large enterprises, ideally having participated in or led digital transformation or modernization programs;
 Advanced English (written and spoken) — non-negotiable;
 Strong technical understanding of IT projects (hands-on mindset);
 Exceptional communication, leadership, and relationship-building skills;
 US resident or valid U.S. Visa and availability to travel once per quarter.

Nice to haves

 Financial Services experience;
 Account Management experience.

Important: after confirming your application on this platform, you’ll receive an email with the next step: completing your application on our internal site, LaunchPod. So keep an eye on your inbox and don’t miss this step — without it, the process can’t move forward.
Perks and benefits

 Professional growth: Accelerate your professional journey with mentorship, TechTalks, and personalized growth roadmaps.
 Competitive compensation: We match your ever-growing skills, talent, and contributions with competitive USD-based compensation and budgets for education, fitness, and team activities.
 A selection of exciting projects: Join projects with modern solutions development and top-tier clients that include Fortune 500 enterprises and leading product brands.
 Flextime: Tailor your schedule for an optimal work-life balance, by having the options of working from home and going to the office, whatever makes you the happiest and most productive.

Job Type: Full-time
Work Location: Remote

